        <mxCell id="1odllvxgz1vKziP6Jo5u-35" value="12.06 Budget &amp;amp; Cost Controlling" style="shape=process;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;backgroundOutline=1;" parent="RDU-i_oViCD79YajCuAX-1" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="-140" y="-356" width="120" height="60" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="1odllvxgz1vKziP6Jo5u-47" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size: 11px;&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 11px;&quot;&gt;Selling (provider) Entity:&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size: 11px;&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 11px;&quot;&gt;No orders need to be issued. Bill can be done trough the pickslips of consumables in the customer entity project.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size: 11px;&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 11px;&quot;&gt;Not recommended for rotables.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size: 11px;&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 11px;&quot;&gt;In the case of rotables it requires the activation of the owner change workflow in the label booking to make sure the installed component belongs to the customer entity. Then if the entity also does the maintenance of the U/S components, now this component is U/S belonging to the selling entity with the customer project and since was a purchase/sell process and not an exchange, then the owner of the rotable in this case should be the customer entity.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size: 11px;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: initial;&quot;&gt;Buying (customer) Entity:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size: 11px;&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 11px;&quot;&gt;Manual booking of the invoice directly to expense account. No impact in average prices and stock value.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="text;html=1;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;whiteSpace=wrap;rounded=0;" parent="RDU-i_oViCD79YajCuAX-1" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="-1093" y="-216" width="477" height="30" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="1odllvxgz1vKziP6Jo5u-49" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size: 11px;&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 11px;&quot;&gt;Selling (Provider) Entity:&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size: 11px;&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 11px;&quot;&gt;Automatic process of creating/booking a Sales Order plus issuing/closing a Bill.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size: 11px;&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 11px;&quot;&gt;Buying (Customer) Entity:&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size: 11px;&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 11px;&quot;&gt;Automatic process of creating/receiving the Purchase Order plus closing of invoice against the bill.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size: 11px;&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 11px;&quot;&gt;This process affects the average price and stock value of the customer entity.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="text;html=1;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;whiteSpace=wrap;rounded=0;" parent="RDU-i_oViCD79YajCuAX-1" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="-483" y="-566" width="284" height="210" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
